    "q-350331": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350331",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{y}^{-8/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{3}{5}{y}^{-5/3}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{5}}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{5}}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{1}^{5}}}) \\\\  & =-3(0-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
